      en: "Givat Shmuel is a city in central Israel, located at an elevation of about 50 meters. It is a suburban community with a population of approximately 27,000 (2022). The city is known for its high standard of living and strong community ties. Geographically, it is situated near the Yarqon River. The economy relies on services and local businesses. Givat Shmuel has a municipal library and several parks. It was named after Rabbi Shmuel Salant, a prominent 19th-century rabbi.",
